WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.063 --> 00:00:06.230
Pollyanna left Mr. Pendleton's house.

2
00:00:06.231 --> 00:00:13.045
As she walked down Pendleton Hill, the sky was filled with storm clouds.

3
00:00:13.046 --> 00:00:16.395
Soon she met Nancy carrying an umbrella.

4
00:00:16.396 --> 00:00:20.017
"Miss Polly was worried you'd get soaked in the rain."

5
00:00:20.018 --> 00:00:24.218
"Oh, I didn't mean to scare her."

6
00:00:24.219 --> 00:00:28.623
"Well, I'm glad she was worried," Nancy said.

7
00:00:28.624 --> 00:00:32.180
Pollyanna was so shocked, she stopped walking.

8
00:00:32.181 --> 00:00:36.361
" Glad that Aunt Polly was worried about

9
00:00:36.362 --> 00:00:40.761
me? Oh, Nancy, that's not how we play the

10
00:00:40.762 --> 00:00:44.749
game." "I wasn't playing the game," Nancy said

11
00:00:44.750 --> 00:00:49.325
sharply. "You don't appreciate what it means that Miss Polly was worried about

12
00:00:49.326 --> 00:00:53.160
you. It means she's becoming

13
00:00:53.161 --> 00:00:56.674
human! She's not just doing her duty all the

14
00:00:56.675 --> 00:01:00.835
time. And she's a better person since you

15
00:01:00.836 --> 00:01:06.694
arrived. She took in that dog and cat, and she's much nicer to me."

16
00:01:06.695 --> 00:01:13.160
Pollyanna hesitated. "Do you think Aunt Polly likes that I live with her?

17
00:01:13.161 --> 00:01:15.923
Would she miss me if I left?"

18
00:01:15.924 --> 00:01:21.466
"Of course she'd miss you! She sent me out with this umbrella.

19
00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:25.135
And she moved you to that pretty bedroom."

20
00:01:25.136 --> 00:01:28.286
Nancy knew her words would please Pollyanna.

21
00:01:28.287 --> 00:01:35.888
But she wasn't prepared for the sudden joy that illuminated Pollyanna's face.

22
00:01:35.889 --> 00:01:39.622
Pollyanna skipped the rest of the way home.

23
00:01:39.623 --> 00:01:43.776
"I couldn't leave Aunt Polly now," she thought.

24
00:01:43.777 --> 00:01:47.583
"I always knew I wanted to live with her.

25
00:01:47.584 --> 00:01:54.786
But I didn't know how much I wanted Aunt Polly to want to live with me!"

26
00:01:54.787 --> 00:01:59.472
*** The next day Pollyanna walked back up Pendleton

27
00:01:59.473 --> 00:02:04.771
Hill. She dreaded telling Mr. Pendleton of her decision to stay with Aunt

28
00:02:04.772 --> 00:02:08.920
Polly. She felt sorry that he lived such a sad, lonely

29
00:02:08.921 --> 00:02:16.106
life. And she suspected that the big, gray house would become cluttered and dusty

30
00:02:16.107 --> 00:02:25.448
again. "If only there was someone else . . . Oh, I have an

31
00:02:25.449 --> 00:02:31.825
idea!" She hurried into Mr. Pendleton's library, where a cheery fire glowed in the

32
00:02:31.826 --> 00:02:35.757
fireplace. "I've thought of the gladdest thing you could

33
00:02:35.758 --> 00:02:40.417
do!" "With you?" Mr. Pendleton said

34
00:02:40.418 --> 00:02:42.174
cautiously. "No,

35
00:02:42.175 --> 00:02:45.145
but—" "You're turning down my

36
00:02:45.146 --> 00:02:48.893
offer?" Pollyanna nodded. "Aunt

37
00:02:48.894 --> 00:02:52.389
Polly—" "Did she refuse to let you

38
00:02:52.390 --> 00:03:01.626
come?" "I—I didn't ask her. I couldn't ask her after I accidentally found out she wants me with

39
00:03:01.627 --> 00:03:11.197
her. And I want to stay too. She's starting to be glad about a lot of things, so I can't leave her now."

40
00:03:11.198 --> 00:03:16.064
There was a long pause with only the crackling fire to break the silence.

41
00:03:16.065 --> 00:03:22.210
"I'm disappointed, but I won't ask you again." Mr. Pendleton spoke in a low voice.

42
00:03:22.211 --> 00:03:30.248
"I have a new idea! You want a partner's hand and heart or a child's presence to make this house a home.

43
00:03:30.249 --> 00:03:34.198
Well, I know another child you could adopt!"

44
00:03:34.199 --> 00:03:42.568
Mr. Pendleton looked outraged by her suggestion. "I don't want another child."

45
00:03:42.569 --> 00:03:45.759
"But you're so kind to other people.

46
00:03:45.760 --> 00:03:53.293
You gave prisms to Mrs. Snow and me, a gold coin to Nancy, money to orphans overseas."

47
00:03:53.294 --> 00:03:57.172
"Pollyanna, listen!" Mr. Pendleton said sharply.

48
00:03:57.173 --> 00:04:03.748
"I've never sent a penny to orphans overseas, and those other gifts were your ideas."

49
00:04:03.749 --> 00:04:08.297
Mr. Pendleton expected Pollyanna to be disappointed in him.

50
00:04:08.298 --> 00:04:11.950
Instead she gleefully clapped her hands.

51
00:04:11.951 --> 00:04:17.808
"I'm so glad! I mean, I'm not glad that you've sent nothing to the orphans.

52
00:04:17.809 --> 00:04:21.029
But I'm glad you can help Jimmy Bean."

53
00:04:21.030 --> 00:04:23.213
"Who's Jimmy Bean?"

54
00:04:23.214 --> 00:04:28.483
"The 'child's presence' that's going to make this place a home.

55
00:04:28.484 --> 00:04:33.766
Poor Jimmy! I had to tell him that my Ladies' Aid out West wouldn't take him.

56
00:04:33.767 --> 00:04:37.712
He'll be so glad to come here!"

57
00:04:37.713 --> 00:04:41.304
"Pollyanna, this is nonsense!"

58
00:04:41.305 --> 00:04:46.847
"You mean you won't take him?" Pollyanna was stunned.

59
00:04:46.848 --> 00:04:48.977
"Correct."

60
00:04:48.978 --> 00:04:53.957
"Fine! I'll find someone else who wants a nice little boy."

61
00:04:53.958 --> 00:04:58.647
Tears of frustration streamed down Pollyanna's face. "I

62
00:04:58.648 --> 00:05:04.488
didn't even get to say he's willing to work." Moved

63
00:05:04.489 --> 00:05:09.263
by her tears, Mr. Pendleton spoke gently. "Why

64
00:05:09.264 --> 00:05:16.834
don't you tell me more about this nice little boy?" ***

65
00:05:16.835 --> 00:05:21.327
The next Saturday Pollyanna and Jimmy visited Mr. Pendleton.

66
00:05:21.328 --> 00:05:28.012
Jimmy was wary about meeting another of Pollyanna's friends.

67
00:05:28.013 --> 00:05:33.975
Having been rejected by Aunt Polly and two Ladies' Aid groups, he wasn't exactly rude.

68
00:05:33.976 --> 00:05:40.055
But when Mr. Pendleton asked him questions, he looked away and gave short answers.

69
00:05:40.056 --> 00:05:47.651
He never once smiled or thanked Mr. Pendleton for inviting him to visit.

70
00:05:47.652 --> 00:05:55.285
After Jimmy left, Pollyanna turned to Mr. Pendleton. "So, are you going to adopt him?"

71
00:05:55.286 --> 00:05:58.949
"I'll think about it," Mr. Pendleton replied.

72
00:05:58.950 --> 00:06:07.882
Pollyanna sighed. That probably meant no.

